From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ole32: linked objects: OleCreateLink*, IOleLink, a link kept in its storage (6005)

OleCreateLink and OleCreateLinkToFile were stubs (E_NOTIMPL), the Ex forms
were missing, OleCreateLinkFromData embedded the data, and the default handler
could not load a linked object's storage (COM-OLELINK).

A linked object is the default handler with IOleLink: its source is named by
a moniker (Set/GetSourceMoniker, Set/GetSourceDisplayName through
MkParseDisplayName), running it binds that moniker (BindToSource: the class
must match unless OLELINKBIND_EVENIFCLASSDIFF; BindIfRunning only for a source
running already; GetBoundSource, UnbindSource), Update binds, updates the
source and refreshes the presentation cache, and the update option is
OLEUPDATE_ALWAYS or OLEUPDATE_ONCALL. Its storage's \1Ole stream holds the
source moniker, class and update option ([MS-OLEDS] 2.3.3 OLEStream), read
back by Load. OleCreateLink[Ex], OleCreateLinkToFile[Ex] (a file moniker,
the file's class from GetClassFile) and OleCreateLinkFromData[Ex] (the data's
"Link Source" moniker; data without one is still embedded) make one, with
its storage, site and cache, brought up to date from the source when it is
to be drawn. Not done: the relative source moniker (written empty, skipped
when read), the update times' use, OLEUPDATE_ALWAYS automatic updates.
